# ==== PURPOSE ====
#
# This test checks the crash window after XA COMMIT or XA ROLLBACK has marked
# the transaction cache entry finalized for SQL XA RECOVER, and before the
# second-phase GTID is added to GTID_EXECUTED. After restart, XA RECOVER and
# GTID_EXECUTED must be in sync when the replica binary log is enabled.
#
# ==== IMPLEMENTATION ====
#
# To reproduce and verify the issue, this test stops the applier at the
# debug-sync point immediately after before-GTID-state-update actions run,
# crashes the replica, restarts it without starting replication, and checks
# recovered XA and GTID state. It does this once for XA COMMIT and once for
# XA ROLLBACK.
#
# Test steps:
#
# 1. Create a source-to-replica GTID topology with replica binary logging.
# 2. Prepare an XA transaction, then run XA COMMIT up to the crash window.
# 3. Crash and restart the replica with the applier stopped.
# 4. Repeat the same crash/recovery check for XA ROLLBACK.
# 5. Let replication continue and clean up.
#
# Test pass conditions:
#
# - After recovery, XA RECOVER does not list the completed XID.
# - Before statement cleanup, the completed XID remains reserved.
# - After recovery, GTID_EXECUTED contains the recovered second-phase GTID.
# - The committed row is present and the rolled-back row is absent.
#
# ==== REFERENCES ====
#
# BUG#36505659: XA RECOVER may list XID after GTID for XA COMMIT or
#               XA ROLLBACK is visible
#
--let $replica_has_binlog = 1
--source common/rpl/rpl_gtid_xa_second_phase_recover_after_gtid_action_crash.inc
